# Root final qualification of the single-qubit static source

Root read the complete independent derivation, its complete finite-check implementation, exposure and launch records, the complete result JSON and original freeze. Root then read the complete separately frozen exposed comparison and verified its reconciliation with the original author proof. The original author source, finite implementation, full raw stdout, launch/result records and scope report have also been read. The source/output freezes are checked by the acceptance recorder. Original text and evidence remain unchanged.

The author and independent arguments support the common added incident-strength construction for one old controlled qubit with genuinely decoupled spectators. Both use an all-sector swap/Casimir gap proof. Their reduction arguments are closely related corrector/integration-by-parts identities; they are not two disjoint mathematical proofs or different-model-family replication. The separate implementations use Pauli Kronecker matrices and computational-basis transitions. Their finite cases and deliberate incorrect variants supplement the all-parameter argument.

The exact original parameter choices give the stated sufficient powers N=O(epsilon^-2), T=O(epsilon^-5), full norm O(epsilon^-2), and action upper bound O(epsilon^-7), with fixed supplied data. The exposed comparison gives an effective refinement when the fixed data are computable: round a rational upper enclosure of the source-size bound and choose rational q within a factor two of its positive allowed minimum. This preserves the powers. Neither an arbitrary oversized N nor an arbitrarily tiny q preserves those upper resource claims. Actual T and the initial complex source phase must be computed from the selected values. The effective refinement is separately attributed; it does not rewrite the author's exact-real existence recipe.

Correction to a broad sentence in the preliminary root review: 'scalar target is free old evolution' applies only to a decomposition with theta=0 and its matching comparison phase. If the supplied decomposition has theta=pi, exp(-i theta0)W=-I; its fixed coherent target retains that minus sign. The main construction handles it. Reparameterizing theta0 changes the stated comparison phase and cannot be done silently. The exposed comparison's r=0 improvement has an exact endpoint and the continuing-action window error; it does not erase that scalar distinction.

The current source acceptance covers the physical single-qubit argument in author sections 2–6, with the qualifications above. Section 8's second-order Sylvester implication is supported only under its full stated finite-matrix and spectral conditions; it constructs no generic bus. Sections 9–10 remain proposals and a diagnostic of sufficient clock estimates. A new root routed-bus proposal is separate, unaccepted work and is not a dependency of this single-qubit result.

Physical premises remain supplied: the source product state and its phase, exact graph/exterior ray, all coefficient/timing/isolation access, and the stated complete initial-state and integrated-generator allowances. Negative-frequency reserves, source motion, every source/old/reference output and the full literal old Hamiltonian are retained. A bound on local incident sums is not a bound on total norm, total reserve, runtime or precision. Fault positivity needs the separate paid margins/positive parameterization already stated.

Author evidence records 12 finite cases and 36 isometry observations, with empty failure list and actual exit 0. The independent record reports 18 finite predicates and three detected defects. Its original launch file lacks cwd and process exit; the exposed comparison retrospectively transcribes the actual command, cwd, session 27634 and tool exit 0 without inventing a resolved interpreter or exact exit timestamp. That provenance limit is preserved. Neither implementation instantiates the enormous small-epsilon resource recipe or validates native hardware.

Disposition: conditional mathematical source acceptance for a publication milestone, with no retained audit and no general coupled-plant or native preparation claim. The publication wrapper and final canonical bytes still require review. No science merge, physical axiom or editable prompt change occurred.
